IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-seat`
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ea3-schedules`
IMPORT `ea3-claims`
IMPORT `ea3-procedure`
IMPORT `ea3-penalties`

-- ============================================================
-- ea1: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation -- cases for the seat layer (Parts 2 to 6, ss 8 to 66).
--
-- Each case asks one seat question with facts a person might give, and states the answer the Act gives.
-- The expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The seat has one seat (an employee or workman), so there are no mirror cases.
-- A case that stays NOTHING says so in its comment; read NOTHING as "the Act does not answer on these facts", never as no.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 10(3): service from 1 January 2024.  Under 26 weeks: 1 day; 26 weeks to under 2 years: 1 week; 2 years to under 5 years: 2 weeks; 5 years or more: 4 weeks.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 7 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2029) TRUE EQUALS JUST 28
-- Not under a contract of service: the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 7 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 10(5): a notice given on 1 March 2026 for 7 days has its last day on 7 March 2026 (the day the notice is given counts).
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), what is the last day of my notice period` (Date 1 3 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST (Date 7 3 2026)

-- s 10(2): where the contract gives no length, the least under s 10(3) is the length (2 years of service: 14 days); where it gives one, that length governs (fork F-10(2), NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), how many days of notice must be given` 0 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), how many days of notice must be given` 3 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST 3

-- s 9(1): a contract for a specified piece of work ends when the work is completed.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), does my contract of service terminate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 12(2): a person under 18 is not bound by a contract that is not for their benefit.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), can my contract of service be enforced against me` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Aged 18: the Act does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), can my contract of service be enforced against me` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 13(2): three days away with no leave and no excuse is deemed a breach, whether or not the employee told the employer; with a reasonable excuse it is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), am I deemed to have broken my contract` 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), am I deemed to have broken my contract` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 14(1): dismissal without notice for misconduct after a due inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer dismiss me without notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Misconduct without an inquiry, or no misconduct: the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer dismiss me without notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer dismiss me without notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 14(2A): a managerial or executive employee dismissed with notice must have served at least 6 months to be a relevant employee.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2A), am I a relevant employee` TRUE `With notice` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2A), am I a relevant employee` TRUE `With notice` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 14(8)(b): during a suspension at least half the salary is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(8), what is the least my employer must pay me during the suspension` 1000 EQUALS 500

-- s 16: the sum is payable for a termination without notice; otherwise the Act does not answer here.
#ASSERT `Under section 16, what sum is the party liable to pay` TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Under section 16, what sum is the party liable to pay` FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 17: a term restricting the right to join a trade union, where no other written law restricts it.
#ASSERT `Under section 17, may a term of my contract restrict my right` `To join a registered trade union` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 3
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 20(2): a salary period of 1 to 31 March 2026 stays within one month; 1 March to 1 April 2026 does not.
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), does my salary period stay within one month` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), does my salary period stay within one month` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 20A: a monthly-rated employee with a gross monthly rate of $3200 who worked 5 of the 20 days required (each of more than 5 hours) is due 5/20 of it: $800.
#ASSERT `Under section 20A, how much salary is due to me for the month` 3200 0 0 20 5 0 EQUALS JUST 800

-- s 21(1): a salary period ending 31 January 2026 is paid before the expiry of the 7th day after it: 7 February 2026.
-- When 7 February is a public holiday the last day moves to the next day that is not a Sunday or a public holiday: 9 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), by what day must my salary be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 2 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), by what day must my salary be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 7 2 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 2 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), was my salary paid in time` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 7 2 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), was my salary paid in time` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 8 2 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 22: dismissed on 5 February 2026 and it was not possible to pay that day: within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday.
-- 8 February is a rest day, so the last day is 7 February.
#ASSERT `Under section 22, by what day must I be paid after dismissal` (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE (Date 8 2 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 2 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 22, by what day must I be paid after dismissal` (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE (Date 8 2 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 2 2026)

-- s 23(3): the most that may be deducted for notice not given is the sum under s 11(1), unless a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise.
#ASSERT `Under section 23(3), what is the most my employer may deduct for the notice I did not give` FALSE 500 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Under section 23(3), what is the most my employer may deduct for the notice I did not give` TRUE 500 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 23(1): salary paid on the day the contract ended, after due notice, is in time; one day later is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 23(1), was my total salary paid on the day my contract ended` TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 23(1), was my total salary paid on the day my contract ended` TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 25(1): paid on a working day, in working hours, at the place of work: yes; if any of the three fails: no.
#ASSERT `Under section 25(1), was my salary paid on a working day, in working hours, at the right place` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 25(1), was my salary paid on a working day, in working hours, at the right place` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- s 27(1)(a): a deduction for absence from work may be made.
#ASSERT `Under section 27(1), is this deduction one that may be made` `For absence from work` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 28(2): a monthly-rated employee absent 2 days of 20 with a day rate of $100 loses at most $200; one not paid by the month with a salary of $1000 loses 2 days of 20, $100.
#ASSERT `Under section 28(2), what is the most my employer may deduct for my absence` TRUE 2 100 2000 20 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `Under section 28(2), what is the most my employer may deduct for my absence` FALSE 2 0 1000 20 EQUALS JUST 100

-- s 29(1): one quarter of one month's wages, or the loss if less, unless the Commissioner permits more.
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), what is the most my employer may deduct for damage or loss I caused` 500 1000 FALSE EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), what is the most my employer may deduct for damage or loss I caused` 200 1000 FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), what is the most my employer may deduct for damage or loss I caused` 500 1000 TRUE EQUALS 500

-- s 31(3): the largest instalment of an advance is one quarter of the salary due.
#ASSERT `Under section 31(3), what is the most that may be deducted in one instalment of an advance` 1000 EQUALS 250

-- s 32(1): deductions of up to half the salary payable are within the limit; one dollar more is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), are the deductions made from my salary within the limit` 1000 2000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), are the deductions made from my salary within the limit` 1001 2000 EQUALS FALSE

-- s 34(2): a first conviction for contravening s 21, 22 or 23 carries a fine of $3000 to $15000 or up to 6 months in prison; a repeat offender faces $6000 to $30000 or up to 12 months.
#ASSERT `Under section 34(2), what is the penalty on my employer` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 3000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 15000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6)
#ASSERT `Under section 34(2), what is the penalty on my employer` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 6000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 30000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)

-- s 34(1): the penalty where the failure is not a contravention of s 21, 22 or 23 is in section 112, which is not among the sources, so the Act's text here does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 34(1), what is the penalty where the failure is not a contravention of section 21, 22 or 23` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 4
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 35: a workman on a salary of $4,500 a month or less is within Part 4; one above is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 35, does Part 4 apply to me` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 35, does Part 4 apply to me` TRUE FALSE 4600 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another employee, not in a managerial or executive position, within $2,600 a month, is within it; one above is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 35, does Part 4 apply to me` FALSE FALSE 2500 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 35, does Part 4 apply to me` FALSE FALSE 2700 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A managerial or executive employee who is not a workman is outside paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `Under section 35, does Part 4 apply to me` FALSE TRUE 2000 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 33(1): the same ceilings decide whether salary has priority: a workman on $4,000 a month is within it.
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), does the rule that my salary is paid before other debts apply to me` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 36(1): a rest day of one whole day without pay, on a Sunday or a day the employer determined, has been allowed.
#ASSERT `Under section 36(1), has my employer allowed me the rest day` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 37(2): rest day worked at the employee's own request, 8 normal hours, day rate $100, hourly rate $20: 8 hours earn one day's basic pay; 3 hours earn half a day.
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my own request` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 8 8 100 20 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my own request` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 3 8 100 20 FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
-- A workman above the ceiling is outside Part 4: the Part gives no answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my own request` TRUE FALSE 4600 0 8 8 100 20 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38(1): the day's limit is 8 hours, or 9 where the contract fixes fewer than 8 hours on some days; the week's limit is 44 hours.
#ASSERT `Under section 38(1), what is the limit of hours in one day` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `Under section 38(1), what is the limit of hours in one day` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 9
#ASSERT `Under section 38(1), what is the limit of hours in one week` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 44

-- s 38(4): 3 hours of overtime at an hourly basic rate of $20, at the employer's request, earn at least 1.5 times the rate: $90.
#ASSERT `Under section 38(4), what is the least payment due for the extra work` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 3 20 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 90

-- s 41: the week holding Wednesday 4 February 2026 starts on Sunday 1 February and ends on Saturday 7 February.
#ASSERT `Under section 41, on what date does the week begin` (Date 4 2 2026) EQUALS Date 1 2 2026
#ASSERT `Under section 41, on what date does the week end` (Date 4 2 2026) EQUALS Date 7 2 2026

-- s 45: dismissed for redundancy after under 2 years of service (1 January 2024 to 31 December 2025): no retrenchment benefit under the section.
#ASSERT `Under section 45, am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Two years or more of service: the Act does not answer here.
#ASSERT `Under section 45, am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 47(2): a sum of $5,000 payable as if retired, where the collective agreement is deemed to contain the provision, must be paid.
#ASSERT `Under section 47(2), what sum must I be paid` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000

-- s 48(4): the penalty is in section 112, which is not among the sources, so the Act's text here does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(4), what is the penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 48(3): an annual wage supplement above one month's wages ($2000 against $1500), where the employer paid none before 26 August 1988, may not be provided for.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(3), may my contract or collective agreement provide for the annual wage supplement` TRUE FALSE 4000 0 FALSE (Date 1 9 1988) 2000 1500 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 5
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 54: a contract of a workman making the salary payable otherwise than in legal tender is illegal and void.
#ASSERT `Under section 54, is my contract of service illegal and void` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a workman: the Part is for workmen and the Act does not answer here.
#ASSERT `Under section 54, is my contract of service illegal and void` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 57: salary $3000 less lawful deductions $200 leaves $2800 due; $2500 paid in legal tender leaves $300 to recover.
#ASSERT `Under section 57, what amount of salary am I entitled to recover` TRUE 3000 200 2500 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `Under section 57, what amount of salary am I entitled to recover` TRUE 3000 200 3000 EQUALS JUST 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 6
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 65: the principal is liable for salary due to a contractor's workman, except in constructional work unless the principal is also a constructional contractor.
#ASSERT `Under section 65, is the principal liable to pay my salary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 65, is the principal liable to pay my salary` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 65, is the principal liable to pay my salary` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 65(2A): salary due on 1 March 2026; 60 days after is 30 April 2026; a public holiday on 30 April moves the last day to 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 65(2A), by what date must I submit the mediation request` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 65(2A), by what date must I submit the mediation request` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2026)

-- s 65(1A): the most a principal who is not the employer is liable for is the salary due, up to one month's salary.
#ASSERT `Under section 65(1A), what is the most the principal or contractor is liable for` FALSE 5000 2000 EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `Under section 65(1A), what is the most the principal or contractor is liable for` FALSE 1500 2000 EQUALS JUST 1500

-- s 66(4): a name changed on 1 March 2026 is to be reported within 7 days, by 9 March 2026 (the last day moved because 8 March is a Sunday).
#ASSERT `Under section 66(4), by what date must the contractor apply for re-registration` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)

-- s 66(7): the penalty is in section 112, which is not among the sources, so the Act's text here does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 66(7), what is the penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cases added so that every seat question has a case: Part 2 (ss 8 to 19).
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act, not from the output.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 8: a term of my contract that sets a condition of service and is less favourable than the Act prescribes is illegal and void; a term that is not less favourable: the Act does not say it is valid.
#ASSERT `Under section 8, is a term of my contract of service void` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 8, is a term of my contract of service void` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(2): a contract for an unspecified period is deemed to run until terminated by either party under Part 2.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(2), is my contract of service deemed to run` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 9(2), is my contract of service deemed to run` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A contract for a specified period: the subsection does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(2), is my contract of service deemed to run` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(1) outside the cases above: the work is not yet completed ("terminates when" counts as "where"), so the contract does not end on that ground.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), does my contract of service terminate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A contract for neither a piece of work nor a period: subsection (1) does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), does my contract of service terminate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10(1): a party may give notice at any time.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(1), may the party give the other party notice at any time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(1), may the party give the other party notice at any time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10(2) with s 8: service from 1 January 2024, notice on 1 January 2026 (2 years: 14 days); a contract term of 7 days is shorter and less favourable, so it is void by 7 days; a contract term of 21 days is not shorter.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), by how many days is my contract's notice term void` 7 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `Under section 10(2), by how many days is my contract's notice term void` 21 (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10(4): a party may waive the party's own right to notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), may the party waive the party's right to notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), may the party waive the party's right to notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10(5): the notice may be given at any time.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), may the notice be given on the day` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 10(5): "The notice must be written": a written notice is; an oral notice is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the notice written` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 7 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the notice written` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 7 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 11(1): paid by the month and a notice period under a month: the gross rate of pay for one day, for each day (10 days at 120 is 1200).
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), what sum must be paid` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 10 9999 120 EQUALS JUST 1200
-- Paid by the month with a notice period of a month or more (40 days from 1 March): the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued during the period.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), what sum must be paid` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 40 4000 100 EQUALS JUST 4000
-- Not paid by the month: the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued during the period of the notice (7 days: 700).
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), what sum must be paid` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 700 0 EQUALS JUST 700
-- Paid by the month, a period under a month, and a day rate I do not know: the Third Schedule's answer is not given.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), what sum must be paid` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 10 9999 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(1): a party who pays the sum may end the contract without notice; one who does not: the Act does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), may the party end the contract without notice by paying the sum` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(1), may the party end the contract without notice by paying the sum` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(2): "in the event of any wilful breach" (read as "where": fork F-EVENT): a wilful breach, yes; none, no.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(2), may the party end the contract without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(2), may the party end the contract without notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(1): a person below 18 is competent to enter into a contract of service; an adult: the subsection does not speak of one.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(1), am I competent to enter into a contract of service` 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(1), am I competent to enter into a contract of service` 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(2): no damages or indemnity are recoverable from a person below 18 unless the contract is for their benefit.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), can damages or indemnity be recovered from me` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), can damages or indemnity be recovered from me` 17 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), can damages or indemnity be recovered from me` 25 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(1): an employer who fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3 is deemed to have broken the contract; one who pays is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), is my employer deemed to have broken my contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), is my employer deemed to have broken my contract` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(1)(a): after a due inquiry into misconduct the employer may down-grade instead of dismissing; without misconduct the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer instantly down-grade me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer instantly down-grade me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1)(b): suspension without pay for not more than one week (7 days) instead of dismissing; 8 days is outside the period; no misconduct: the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer suspend me without pay` TRUE TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer suspend me without pay` TRUE TRUE 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may my employer suspend me without pay` FALSE TRUE 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(2): an employee not in a managerial or executive position is a relevant employee; who considers the dismissal was without just cause may lodge a claim for reinstatement or compensation (the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open).
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` Yes FALSE `With notice` 12 TRUE Yes `Compensation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An employee who does not consider the dismissal was without just cause or excuse: the "where" is unmet.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` Yes FALSE `With notice` 12 FALSE Yes `Compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not dismissed at all.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` No FALSE `With notice` 12 TRUE Yes `Compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A managerial employee dismissed with notice after only 3 months is not a relevant employee (6 months needed).
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` Yes TRUE `With notice` 3 TRUE Yes `Compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure whether the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open: that Act is not among the sources.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` Yes FALSE `With notice` 12 TRUE `I am not sure` `Compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A remedy the subsection does not list ("either of the following remedies").
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may I lodge a claim for wrongful dismissal` Yes FALSE `With notice` 12 TRUE Yes `A sum the Commissioner considers just` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(3)(a): a Tribunal satisfied of dismissal without just cause may direct reinstatement in a claim for reinstatement.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` Yes TRUE `To be reinstated in my job` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not satisfied; or not a Tribunal: an unmet "if".
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` Yes FALSE `To be reinstated in my job` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` No TRUE `To be reinstated in my job` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure the body is the Tribunal; or a claim for compensation, not reinstatement.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` `I am not sure` TRUE `To be reinstated in my job` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` Yes TRUE `Compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(3)(b): in a claim for compensation the Tribunal satisfied may direct payment of compensation.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to pay me compensation` Yes TRUE `Compensation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Tribunal direct my employer to pay me compensation` Yes FALSE `Compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(8)(a): suspension while an inquiry is held, up to one week, or a longer period the Commissioner determines (0 means none was determined).
#ASSERT `Under section 14(8), may my employer suspend me while an inquiry is held` 7 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(8), may my employer suspend me while an inquiry is held` 8 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(8), may my employer suspend me while an inquiry is held` 10 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(8), may my employer suspend me while an inquiry is held` 15 14 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(9): if the inquiry does not disclose any misconduct the employer must immediately restore the full amount withheld; if it does, no.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(9), must my employer immediately restore the salary withheld` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(9), must my employer immediately restore the salary withheld` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(9), how much salary must my employer restore` TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 500
-- Misconduct was disclosed: the subsection states no amount.
#ASSERT `Under section 14(9), how much salary must my employer restore` FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15: the employee, or a dependant, immediately threatened by danger to the person by violence or disease that the employee did not undertake to run.
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` TRUE No TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` FALSE Yes TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A cousin is not a dependant.
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` FALSE No TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A danger I took on by my contract, or one that is not immediate.
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` TRUE No TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` TRUE No FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure whether the person is a dependant: the definition may give no answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 15, may I leave my job without notice because of danger` FALSE `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 16: the party who breaks the contract is liable to pay the sum, subject to anything in the contract to the contrary.
#ASSERT `Under section 16, is the party who broke my contract liable to pay the sum` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 16, is the party who broke my contract liable to pay the sum` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 16, is the party who broke my contract liable to pay the sum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18(1), (2), (3): a change of employer of the kinds named does not break the continuity of the period of employment, and the earlier period counts.
#ASSERT `Under section 18(1), does the change of employer break the continuity of my employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(1), does the change of employer break the continuity of my employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), does my employer's death break the continuity of my employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), does my employer's death break the continuity of my employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), does a change in those who employ me break the continuity of my employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), does a change in those who employ me break the continuity of my employment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 18(1), does my period of employment count with the other body corporate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(1), does my period of employment count with the other body corporate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), does my period of employment count with the personal representatives or trustees` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(2), does my period of employment count with the personal representatives or trustees` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), does my period of employment count after the change` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18(3), does my period of employment count after the change` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A(1)(a): a transfer of the undertaking does not end the contract of a person employed in the part transferred.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does the transfer end my contract of service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does the transfer end my contract of service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 18A(1)(b): the period of employment in the part transferred counts with the transferee; if nothing was transferred, "If an undertaking ... is transferred" is unmet; a person not employed in the part transferred is not one the paragraph speaks of.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my period of employment count as a period with the new employer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my period of employment count as a period with the new employer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my period of employment count as a period with the new employer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(1)(a): the contract has effect after the transfer as if originally made with the transferee.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my contract have effect with the new employer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my contract have effect with the new employer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does my contract have effect with the new employer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(1)(b): the transfer does not break the continuity of the period of employment.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does the transfer break the continuity of my employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(1), does the transfer break the continuity of my employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(2): on completion of the transfer the transferor's rights, powers, duties and liabilities under the preserved contract pass to the transferee, and earlier acts and omissions are deemed done by or in relation to the transferee ("on completion of" read as "upon": fork F-EVENT).
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the transferor's right, power, duty or liability transferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the transferor's right, power, duty or liability transferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the transferor's right, power, duty or liability transferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done by the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done by the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done by the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(3): on completion of the transfer the terms and conditions of a preserved contract are the same as those enjoyed immediately before.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(3), are my terms and conditions of service the same after the transfer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(3), are my terms and conditions of service the same after the transfer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(3), are my terms and conditions of service the same after the transfer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(4): subsections (1) and (2) do not transfer or affect the liability to be prosecuted for an offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(4), do subsections (1) and (2) transfer or affect the liability` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(4), do subsections (1) and (2) transfer or affect the liability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(5): the transferor must notify before a transfer takes place; no transfer: the duty is not spoken of (fork F-NODUTY).
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), must the transferor notify the affected employees and their trade union` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), must the transferor notify the affected employees and their trade union` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(5): told on 1 March for a transfer on 10 March, as soon as it was reasonable: in time; told on the day of the transfer, or not as soon as reasonable: not.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), did the transferor tell the affected employees in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), did the transferor tell the affected employees in time` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), did the transferor tell the affected employees in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A(5)(a), (b), (c): a notification of all three matters; one that leaves a matter out: the Act does not say what follows.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), is the notification of all the matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(5), is the notification of all the matters` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(8): a trade union the transferor recognised, for an employee who becomes the transferee's employee, is deemed recognised by the transferee if the majority of its employees are members; in any other case only for representing the employee on a dispute; if the "Where" is unmet, no.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8), is my trade union deemed to be recognised by the transferee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8), is my trade union deemed to be recognised by the transferee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8), is my trade union deemed to be recognised by the transferee` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A(9): a dispute between the transferor or transferee and an employee arising from the transfer may be referred to the Commissioner.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(9), may a party refer the dispute to the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(9), may a party refer the dispute to the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(12): nothing in the section prevents the transferee and the employee or union from negotiating different terms.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(12), may the parties negotiate different terms of service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(12), may the parties negotiate different terms of service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(8A): a collective agreement continues for 18 months after the transfer (a transfer on 1 March 2026: to 1 September 2027), or until its expiry if that is later.
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8A), until what date does the collective agreement continue` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS Date 1 9 2027
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8A), until what date does the collective agreement continue` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 12 2027) EQUALS Date 1 12 2027
#ASSERT `Under section 18A(8A), until what date does the collective agreement continue` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS Date 1 9 2027
-- s 19: an employer who enters into a contract of service or collective agreement contrary to Part 2 is guilty of an offence; the penalty is in section 112, which is not among the sources.
#ASSERT `Under section 19, is my employer guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19, is my employer guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 19, what is the penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 19, what is the penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cases added so that every seat question has a case: Part 3 (ss 20 to 34).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 20(3): in the absence of a salary period so fixed the salary period is deemed to be one month.
#ASSERT `Under section 20(3), is my salary period deemed to be one month` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(3), is my salary period deemed to be one month` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 20A(1): a monthly-rated employee who did not complete a whole month because they started after the first day, or took unpaid leave; for none of the reasons, or if not paid by the month, the "If" is unmet.
#ASSERT `Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month worked out by the formula` TRUE `I started work after the first day of the month` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month worked out by the formula` TRUE `I took unpaid leave for one or more days of the month` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month worked out by the formula` TRUE `None of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month worked out by the formula` FALSE `I started work after the first day of the month` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(2): additional payments for overtime must be paid not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period (31 March 2026: 14 April 2026, a Tuesday; a public holiday on that day moves it to the next day).
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), by what day must my payments for overtime be paid` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), by what day must my payments for overtime be paid` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), were my payments for overtime paid in time` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), were my payments for overtime paid in time` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), were my payments for overtime paid in time` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(3): salary paid on completion of the contract of service: on the day it was completed, yes; a day later, no.
#ASSERT `Under section 21(3), was my total salary paid when my contract was completed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(3), was my total salary paid when my contract was completed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 22: dismissed on Monday 2 March 2026; paid the same day: in time. If it was not possible to pay that day, within 3 days after on a day that is not a rest day or holiday: 3 March yes; 3 March a rest day no; 6 March (4 days after) no.
#ASSERT `Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) TRUE (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 23(2): an employee who leaves without notice is paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day they leave (left Monday 2 March 2026: 9 March 2026, a Monday); a public holiday on the 9th moves it to the 10th.
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), by what date must my total salary be paid` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), by what date must my total salary be paid` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), was my total salary paid in time` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), was my total salary paid in time` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An employee who left after giving due notice: subsection (2) does not speak of them.
#ASSERT `Under section 23(2), was my total salary paid in time` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(1): no payment of salary on termination of service without the Comptroller's permission; with permission the Act does not say it may be paid.
#ASSERT `Under section 24(1), may my employer pay me without the Comptroller's permission` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(1), may my employer pay me without the Comptroller's permission` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(2): payment must not be delayed more than 30 days after the Comptroller received the notice (received 1 March 2026: 31 March 2026).
#ASSERT `Under section 24(2), by what day must I be paid after the Comptroller has been told` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 24(2), was my payment delayed no more than 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(2), was my payment delayed no more than 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 25(2): subsection (1) does not apply where the salary is paid into a bank account in Singapore in the employee's name; otherwise (1) is a general rule and applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 25(2), does section 25(1) apply to my salary` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 25(2), does section 25(1) apply to my salary` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(1): no deduction is to be made unless the Act authorises it or one of the listed authorities requires it; a deduction with no such authority: no; with one: the Act does not itself say it is allowed.
#ASSERT `Under section 26(1), may my employer make this deduction` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 26(1), may my employer make this deduction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(1B): an employee cannot be penalised for withdrawing a written consent to a deduction under (d), (e), (i) or (j); a deduction of another kind: the subsection does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 27(1B), can I be penalised for withdrawing my consent` `For house accommodation my employer supplied` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(1B), can I be penalised for withdrawing my consent` `For absence from work` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 27(1B), can I be penalised for withdrawing my consent` `For house accommodation my employer supplied` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(2): "services" does not include the supply of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of employment.
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is the supply a service` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is the supply a service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(3): "employment benefit" means a benefit derived from being employed, other than salary, and includes annual leave beyond section 88A and flexible benefits; salary is not one, and a thing outside all of these: the class is not closed.
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), is the thing an employment benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), is the thing an employment benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), is the thing an employment benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3), is the thing an employment benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(3)(b)(i): 20 days of leave given against an entitlement of 14 days under section 88A: 6 days beyond; 10 given: none beyond; an entitlement I do not know (0): the section 88A answer is not given.
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3)(b)(i), how many days of annual leave beyond section 88A did I get` 20 14 EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3)(b)(i), how many days of annual leave beyond section 88A did I get` 10 14 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under section 27(3)(b)(i), how many days of annual leave beyond section 88A did I get` 20 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28(1): deductions for absence only for absence from the place where required to work, during the time required to work.
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may my employer deduct from my salary for my absence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may my employer deduct from my salary for my absence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 28(3): if an employee is absent otherwise than as the Act or the contract allows, the employer may deduct the cost of food supplied during the absence, subject to a court's or the Commissioner's order.
#ASSERT `Under section 28(3), may my employer deduct the cost of food supplied to me while I was absent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(3), may my employer deduct the cost of food supplied to me while I was absent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(3), may my employer deduct the cost of food supplied to me while I was absent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29(1): a deduction for damage or loss must not be made until the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause; after it, the Act does not say it may be made.
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), may my employer make the deduction for damage or loss now` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), may my employer make the deduction for damage or loss now` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30(2): at most the value supplied, and with other such deductions at most one-quarter of the salary payable for the period (salary 2000: 500; 200 already deducted: 300 left; the value 800 is more, so 300; a value of 100 is the least).
#ASSERT `Under section 30(2), what is the most my employer may deduct for accommodation, an amenity or a service` 800 200 2000 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `Under section 30(2), what is the most my employer may deduct for accommodation, an amenity or a service` 100 0 2000 EQUALS 100
-- s 30(3): a deduction under section 27(1)(e) is subject to conditions the Commissioner may impose; one under (d): the subsection does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 30(3), is the deduction subject to conditions the Commissioner may impose` `For an amenity or service my employer supplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 30(3), is the deduction subject to conditions the Commissioner may impose` `For house accommodation my employer supplied` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 31(1): recovery of an advance made before the contract began is to begin from the first payment of salary for a completed salary period.
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), may my employer start recovering the advance from this payment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), may my employer start recovering the advance from this payment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), may my employer start recovering the advance from this payment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 31(1): no recovery may be made of an advance made for travelling expenses; for another advance the subsection says when recovery begins, not that it may be made.
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), may my employer recover an advance made for my travelling expenses` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(1), may my employer recover an advance made for my travelling expenses` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 31(2): advances may be recovered in instalments spread over not more than 12 months.
#ASSERT `Under section 31(2), is my advance being recovered over a permitted number of months` 12 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(2), is my advance being recovered over a permitted number of months` 13 EQUALS FALSE
-- s 31(4): loans may be recovered in instalments by deductions from salary.
#ASSERT `Under section 31(4), may the loan be recovered in instalments by deductions from my salary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 31(4), may the loan be recovered in instalments by deductions from my salary` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 31(5): an instalment of a loan must not exceed one-quarter of the salary due for the period (2000: 500).
#ASSERT `Under section 31(5), what is the most that may be deducted in one instalment of a loan` 2000 EQUALS 500
-- s 32(1): the total of the deductions in a salary period must not exceed 50% of the salary payable (2000: 1000).
#ASSERT `Under section 32(1), what is the largest total of deductions in the salary period` 2000 EQUALS 1000
-- s 32(2): subsection (1) does not apply to deductions from the last salary due on termination or completion of the contract.
#ASSERT `Under section 32(2), does the limit in section 32(1) apply to a deduction from my last salary` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 32(2), does the limit in section 32(1) apply to a deduction from my last salary` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 33(3): the priority rule applies only to property the employees were working on, the produce of their work, movable property they used, and money due to the employer for work they did.
#ASSERT `Under section 33(3), does the rule apply to the property or money` `Property my fellow workers and I were working on` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(3), does the rule apply to the property or money` `Money due to my employer for work we did` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(3), does the rule apply to the property or money` `Property or money of some other kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33(4): the amount payable to each employee must not exceed 5 months' salary (a month's salary of 3000: 15000).
#ASSERT `Under section 33(4), what is the most I can be paid in priority` 20000 3000 EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `Under section 33(4), what is the most I can be paid in priority` 6000 3000 EQUALS 6000
-- s 33(7): "employees" is deemed to include subcontractors for labour, and "salary" money due to one; a person outside both: the class is not closed.
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), am I an employee for the purposes of section 33` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), am I an employee for the purposes of section 33` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), am I an employee for the purposes of section 33` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), is the sum salary for the purposes of section 33` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), is the sum salary for the purposes of section 33` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(7), is the sum salary for the purposes of section 33` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 34(1): an employer who fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3 is guilty of an offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 34(1), is my employer guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 34(1), is my employer guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 34, is my employer guilty of an offence under section 21, 22 or 23` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 34, is my employer guilty of an offence under section 21, 22 or 23` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cases added so that every seat question has a case: Part 4 (ss 35 to 53).
-- In these cases a workman on a basic pay of 3000 a month with no commissions is within Part 4 (s 35(a): not more than $4,500 a month).
-- A managerial employee who is not a workman is outside it (s 35(b)), and Part 4 does not speak of them.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 36(2): a shift worker's employer may substitute a continuous period of 30 hours as the rest day; a shorter period, or a worker not on shift work, is not covered (fork F-36(2)).
#ASSERT `Under section 36(2), may my employer substitute a continuous period as my rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 36(2), may my employer substitute a continuous period as my rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE 29 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 36(2), may my employer substitute a continuous period as my rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside Part 4.
#ASSERT `Under section 36(2), may my employer substitute a continuous period as my rest day` FALSE TRUE 3000 0 TRUE 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 36(3): a 30-hour period beginning before 6 p.m. on a Sunday for a shift worker is deemed within the week; one beginning at 6 p.m., or not on a Sunday, leaves the "Where" unmet.
#ASSERT `Under section 36(3), is my rest day deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE TRUE 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 36(3), is my rest day deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE TRUE 18 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 36(3), is my rest day deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE FALSE 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 36(4): where the employer determines the rest day, the roster must be prepared before the month begins (roster on 25 February for March: in time; on 1 March: not); where the employer does not determine it, the duty does not arise (fork F-NODUTY).
#ASSERT `Under section 36(4), was my rest-day roster prepared before the month began` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE (Date 25 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 36(4), was my rest-day roster prepared before the month began` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 36(4), was my rest-day roster prepared before the month began` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE (Date 25 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37(1): an employee must not be compelled to work on a rest day unless engaged in continuous shift work, or in a case section 38(2) or 40(2A) allows.
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), may I be compelled to work on a rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), may I be compelled to work on a rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), may I be compelled to work on a rest day` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 37(3): worked a rest day at the employer's request, normal hours 8, a day's basic rate 100, an hourly rate 12.50: up to 4 hours: one day's pay (100); more than 4 up to 8 hours: 2 days' pay (200); 10 hours: 200 plus one and a half times the hourly rate for the 2 hours over (37.50), 237.50; a written order under section 41A(2) that the entitlement does not apply: the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under section 37(3), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my employer's request` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 4 8 100 12.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under section 37(3), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my employer's request` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 6 8 100 12.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `Under section 37(3), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my employer's request` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 10 8 100 12.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 237.5
#ASSERT `Under section 37(3), what is the least sum payable for a rest day I worked at my employer's request` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 10 8 100 12.5 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37(3A)(a): "normal hours of work" are the usual hours agreed (not above the limit), or 8 hours a day if nothing is agreed (0 means nothing agreed); agreed hours above the limit: the Act does not answer.
