#ASSERT `Under section 65(2C)(b), do the old rules still apply to my claim` TRUE (Date 1 4 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 65(2C)(b), do the old rules still apply to my claim` FALSE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 65(3), (4): nothing in the section prevents a person who paid salary on a claim from suing the employer, or a workman from recovering from the employer instead.
#ASSERT `Under section 65(3), does the section prevent the person from suing the employer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 65(3), does the section prevent the person from suing the employer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 65(4), does the section prevent me from recovering from my employer instead` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 65(4), does the section prevent me from recovering from my employer instead` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 65(5): the reference to principal includes the Government or a statutory body acting in the discharge of its functions; the class is not closed.
#ASSERT `Under section 65(5), is the person a principal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 65(5), is the person a principal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(1): after the Minister requires registration, a person must not act as a contractor or subcontractor unless registered; a registered person: the Act does not say they may; before the Minister requires it: not covered here (the bar is its own question in layer 1).
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), may the person act as a contractor or subcontractor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), may the person act as a contractor or subcontractor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), may the person act as a contractor or subcontractor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(2): every application for registration must be in the prescribed form; one that is not: no; one that is: the Act does not say it is accepted.
#ASSERT `Under section 66(2), is the application for registration acceptable` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(2), is the application for registration acceptable` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(3): a person registered as a contractor or subcontractor is deemed to be the employer of the workmen they employ.
#ASSERT `Under section 66(3), is the person deemed to be the employer of the workmen` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(3), is the person deemed to be the employer of the workmen` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(4): a registered contractor who changes name applies within 7 days of the change (changed on Monday 2 March 2026: by Monday 9 March 2026).
#ASSERT `Under section 66(4), was the application for re-registration made in time` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(4), was the application for re-registration made in time` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(4), was the application for re-registration made in time` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(7): a person who contravenes section 66 is guilty of an offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 66(7), is the person guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(7), is the person guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cases for the seat questions that ask the bars and yes/no twins written with the rulings of 2026-11-05.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 12(2): no contract of service as an employee is enforceable against a person below 18 unless it is for their benefit; a person aged 17 on a contract not for their benefit is barred, one on a contract for their benefit is not, and a person aged 18 is outside the subsection (it speaks of "a person below 18 years of age").
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the enforcement of my contract of service against me barred` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the enforcement of my contract of service against me barred` 17 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the enforcement of my contract of service against me barred` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(2): the same for damages or indemnity "recoverable from that person in respect of the contract of service".
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the recovery of damages or indemnity from me barred` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the recovery of damages or indemnity from me barred` 17 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), is the recovery of damages or indemnity from me barred` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29(1): "No deduction ... shall be made until the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause": barred until the opportunity is given, not barred after.
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), is my employer barred from making the deduction for damage or loss` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), is my employer barred from making the deduction for damage or loss` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 41A(3): where the Commissioner has exempted or directed, the employer must display the order; with neither, there is nothing to display; a workman above the ceiling is outside Part 4.
#ASSERT `Under section 41A(3), must my employer display the order` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 41A(3), must my employer display the order` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 41A(3), must my employer display the order` TRUE FALSE 5000 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 48(3): the cap binds a contract made on or after 26 August 1988 of an employer that paid no annual wage supplement before then; an employer that paid one before, or a contract made before the date, is outside it.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(3), does the cap of one month's wages apply to my contract or collective agreement` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48(3), does the cap of one month's wages apply to my contract or collective agreement` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48(3), does the cap of one month's wages apply to my contract or collective agreement` TRUE FALSE 3000 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 1980) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 65(1): "where salary is claimed from the principal, this Act (with the exception of section 33 relating to priority of salary) applies": section 33 does not apply to a claim on the principal; a salary not claimed from the principal is outside the exception.
#ASSERT `Under section 65(1), does section 33 on the priority of salary apply to my salary claimed from the principal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 65(1), does section 33 on the priority of salary apply to my salary claimed from the principal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 66(1): the bar begins with the Minister's notification and ends once the person is registered; before the notification there is no bar.
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), is the person barred from acting as a contractor or subcontractor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), is the person barred from acting as a contractor or subcontractor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 66(1), is the person barred from acting as a contractor or subcontractor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ============================================================
-- ea2: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ea2-seat.l4 (Employment Act 1968, Parts 6A to 14, with the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting)
-- Notification 2019).  Each case states the facts a real person in the seat would give, and the answer the text gives.
-- Expected values were decided from the text of the section, and written down, before the question was run.  Dates were worked
-- out on a calendar.  Each question has at least one case; check.sh counts the assertions written in each case file and requires every one to be satisfied.


§ `Part 6A -- part-time employees (s 66A)`

-- 30 hours, no declaration: part-time (s 66A(1): less than 35 hours)
#ASSERT `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` `ea2 seat: Yes` 30 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 34.5 hours is less than 35
#ASSERT `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` `ea2 seat: Yes` 34.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- exactly 35 hours is not less than 35: the definition says no
#ASSERT `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` `ea2 seat: Yes` 35 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 30 hours but the Minister has declared the class not to be regarded as part-time (s 66A(2))
#ASSERT `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` `ea2 seat: Yes` 30 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not sure whether an employee: the Act does not answer
#ASSERT `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` `ea2 seat: I am not sure` 30 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part 7 -- domestic workers (s 67)`

-- a notification applies the provision to domestic workers like me
#ASSERT `Under section 67, does a provision of the Act apply to me as a domestic worker` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no notification: the section does not say the Act does not apply to me; the Act does not answer
#ASSERT `Under section 67, does a provision of the Act apply to me as a domestic worker` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

