#ASSERT `Under paragraph 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the form of the retrenchment report meet the Notification` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- information missing: not every requirement met
#ASSERT `Under paragraph 3(2), 4 and 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, did my employer meet every requirement concerning the retrenchment report` `ea2 seat: No` TRUE `ea2 seat: Yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not in time: not every requirement met
#ASSERT `Under paragraph 3(2), 4 and 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, did my employer meet every requirement concerning the retrenchment report` `ea2 seat: I am not sure` FALSE `ea2 seat: Yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- all three met: no sentence of the Notification says the employer complied (NOTES.md finding), so the Act does not answer yes
#ASSERT `Under paragraph 3(2), 4 and 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, did my employer meet every requirement concerning the retrenchment report` `ea2 seat: Yes` TRUE `ea2 seat: Yes` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ============================================================
-- ea3: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- ea3: CASES FOR THE EMPLOYEE'S SEAT (ea3-seat.l4).
-- Each case states the facts a real employee would give, and the expected answer is worked out by hand from the text cited beside the group,
-- never copied from what the code printed.  Every question of the seat is asked at least once, and a NOTHING case is asserted wherever the Act is silent.
-- Calendar facts the cases rely on: 1 June 2025 is a Sunday, so 2 June 2025 is a Monday and 16 June 2025 is a Monday.  No public holiday is passed by the seat.

-- s 115(1A) (lines 4629-4636): a dispute of a prescribed type, or a claim lodged before 1 April 2017.
-- Of a prescribed type: the Commissioner is not barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 Yes` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not of a prescribed type, but the claim was lodged on 31 March 2017, before 1 April 2017.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 No` TRUE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A claim lodged on 1 April 2017 is not "before 1 April 2017".
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 No` TRUE (Date 1 4 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 No` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure whether the type is prescribed, and no claim before 1 April 2017: it is yes if prescribed and no if not, so the answer is not given.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 I am not sure` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not sure, but the claim was lodged before 1 April 2017: the answer is yes whichever way the type is.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` `ea3 I am not sure` TRUE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 115(2) (lines 4640-4648): one year before the claim or the termination; the proviso of 6 months.
-- A matter of 1 June 2025, a claim lodged 15 June 2025: one year before is 15 June 2024.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 15 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter of 1 June 2024 is earlier than 15 June 2024.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 15 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Out of a termination on 10 June 2025: lodged on 10 December 2025 it is within 6 months.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 10 12 2025) TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Lodged on 11 December 2025 it is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 11 12 2025) TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The text does not say which event the year is counted from: from the claim (20 June 2024) the matter is barred, from the termination (10 June 2024) it is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` (Date 15 6 2024) (Date 20 6 2025) TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 115(1), with (1A) and (2) (lines 4619-4648): whether the Commissioner can decide the dispute.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer` TRUE TRUE `ea3 Yes` TRUE (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Barred by (2): the matter is earlier than one year before the claim.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer` TRUE TRUE `ea3 Yes` TRUE (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2024) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure whether the type is prescribed, and the claim was lodged after 31 March 2017: yes if prescribed, no if not.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer` TRUE TRUE `ea3 I am not sure` TRUE (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A dispute not with an employer or a person liable: the Act gives the Commissioner no power and does not say there is none.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer` FALSE TRUE `ea3 Yes` TRUE (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 115(2A) (lines 4651-4656)
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2A), can the Commissioner direct me and my employer to attend mediation or conciliation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2A), can the Commissioner direct me and my employer to attend mediation or conciliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 115(2A), can the Commissioner direct me and my employer to attend mediation or conciliation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 115(3) (lines 4659-4667)
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3), can the Commissioner decide my claim as a subcontractor for labour against the contractor or subcontractor` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3), can the Commissioner decide my claim as a subcontractor for labour against the contractor or subcontractor` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 115(3A) (lines 4668-4672): $20,000 for an employee in a managerial or an executive position.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3A), is the sum I claim within the limit on what the Commissioner can order` TRUE 20000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3A), is the sum I claim within the limit on what the Commissioner can order` TRUE 20001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3A), is the sum I claim within the limit on what the Commissioner can order` FALSE 50000 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 115(3B) and (3C) (lines 4673-4684): no later than 14 days after the date of the order.
-- An order on Monday 2 June 2025: the 14th day is Monday 16 June.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` TRUE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` TRUE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order on Sunday 1 June: the 14th day, Sunday 15 June, is excluded, so Monday 16 June is in time (section 50(b) of the Interpretation Act).
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An order that was not made in the employee's absence: this power is not given.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` FALSE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An order on Monday 2 June 2025: 14 days after is Monday 16 June.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), what is the last day on which I can apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` (Date 2 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)
-- An order on Sunday 1 June: the 14th day, Sunday 15 June, is excluded, so Monday 16 June.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3C), what is the last day on which I can apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)

-- s 115(4) (lines 4686-4692)
#ASSERT `Under section 115(4), is the new owner of my employer's undertaking my employer for a claim before the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 115(4), is the new owner of my employer's undertaking my employer for a claim before the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 116(1) and (3) (lines 4696-4730)
-- An order under section 115 for a workman, and the inquiry finds the contract.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Whenever the Commissioner has made an order under section 115" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): no order has been made.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "after inquiry finds that there exists ... a contract" (ruling (b)): no such contract is found.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The sum is payable to an employee who is not a workman or a subcontractor for labour (read as the text's own no, fork F28).
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The salary owed 1,000 less the 600 admitted is 400, within the 500 for which the person is liable under section 65.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 Yes` 500 1000 600 EQUALS JUST 400
-- The balance 400 is more than the 300 for which the person is liable under section 65.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 Yes` 300 1000 600 EQUALS JUST 300
-- The employee does not know the amount for which the person is liable under section 65.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 Yes` 0 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
-- What is admitted is enough: the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 Yes` 300 1000 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 No` 300 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` `ea3 I am not sure` 300 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 117(1) (lines 4739-4748): within 14 days after the decision or order.
#ASSERT `Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision` TRUE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An appeal on 17 June is outside the 14 days the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7).
#ASSERT `Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision` TRUE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A decision on Sunday 1 June: the 14th day is excluded, so Monday 16 June is in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Where any person interested is dissatisfied" (ruling (b)): not dissatisfied.
#ASSERT `Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision` FALSE (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 118(1) (lines 4753-4760)
#ASSERT `Under section 118(1), may the Commissioner charge me a fee other than the registration fee` `s 118(1) the registration fee at the rate in the Second Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 118(1), may the Commissioner charge me a fee other than the registration fee` `s 118(1) a fee of any other kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 119 (lines 4778-4867)
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(a), have I made my claim in a way the Act provides` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(a), have I made my claim in a way the Act provides` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(a), have I made my claim in a way the Act provides` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An inquiry on 10 June, notice on 7 June: 3 days before.
