-- Third Schedule (lines 5540-5696): a piece-rate employee, 14 days before.
-- (1,400 + 100 + 50) / 10 days worked.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates` 1400 100 50 10 EQUALS JUST 155
-- No day worked in the 14 days: the Schedule divides by the days worked and gives no answer for none.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates` 1400 100 50 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Allowances of every kind are left out of the basic rate.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates` 1400 0 10 EQUALS JUST 140

-- Third Schedule item 2: monthly rate, the same number of days in every week.
-- 12 x 2,730 / (52 x 5).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` 2600 0 130 5 0 EQUALS JUST 126
-- 12 x 2,600 / (52 x 5).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` 2600 0 5 0 EQUALS JUST 120
-- Two days of 5 hours or less count as one day (item 7), so 5 days.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` 2600 0 4 2 EQUALS JUST 120
-- 12 x 2,600 / (52 x 3).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` 2600 0 3 0 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` 2600 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Third Schedule item 3: 5 days one week, 4 days (3 and two half days) the next: the average is 4.5.
-- 12 x 2,808 / (52 x 4.5).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks` 2808 0 0 5 0 3 2 EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks` 2808 0 5 0 3 2 EQUALS JUST 144

-- Third Schedule item 4: different numbers of days in different weeks, the average over the 3 weeks before: (5 + 4 + 3) / 3 = 4.
-- 12 x 2,600 / (52 x 4).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` 2600 0 0 5 0 4 0 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 150
-- For salary in lieu of notice the same 3 weeks before the termination.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` 2600 0 0 5 0 4 0 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week` 2600 0 5 0 4 0 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 150

