-- Fifth Schedule (lines 5752-5790)
-- 4 x 5.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 I work the same number of days in every week` 5 0 (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) EQUALS JUST 20
-- 4 x 4.5.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 I work the same number of days in every week` 4 1 (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) EQUALS JUST 18
-- 4 x (5 + 4) / 2.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, in a pattern that repeats over a number of fixed weeks` 0 0 (LIST 5, 4) (LIST 0, 0) (LIST) (LIST) EQUALS JUST 18
-- 4 x 14 / 3 = 18.67, rounded down to the nearest half day (item 5).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, in a pattern that repeats over a number of fixed weeks` 0 0 (LIST 5, 5, 4) (LIST 0, 0, 0) (LIST) (LIST) EQUALS JUST 18.5
-- 4 x 13 / 3 = 17.33, rounded down to 17.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, with no regular pattern` 0 0 (LIST) (LIST) (LIST 5, 4, 4) (LIST 0, 0, 0) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` `ea3 my work pattern is none of these` 0 0 (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) (LIST) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 119(1)(b), (e), (f), (g), (h) and (2)(b) (lines 4785-4867): the steps of a claim, from the employee's side.
-- The memorandum or verbal claim and the registration fee are both received: the duty to summon the employer has arisen.
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(b), is the Commissioner bound to summon my employer in writing once I have made my claim and paid the registration fee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "upon receipt of the memorandum or verbal claim and of the registration fee" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "upon" counts as "where"): without the fee the duty has not arisen.
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(b), is the Commissioner bound to summon my employer in writing once I have made my claim and paid the registration fee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The memorandum or verbal claim is not received (ruling (b)).
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(b), is the Commissioner bound to summon my employer in writing once I have made my claim and paid the registration fee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(e), must I be present at the preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not notified in writing: the text does not say that the party must be present.
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(e), must I be present at the preliminary inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(e), must I be present at the preliminary inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` `s 119(1)(f) amend the whole claim or a portion of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` `s 119(1)(f) withdraw the whole claim or a portion of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` `s 119(1)(f) make a counterclaim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` `s 119(1)(f) reach a settlement in respect of the claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The four steps are named and the list is not closed with "only".
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` `s 119(1)(f) a step of some other kind` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(g), will the Commissioner record the terms of our settlement in an order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if a settlement is effected at a preliminary inquiry" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(g), will the Commissioner record the terms of our settlement in an order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(h), must I attend the hearing and state my case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(1)(h), must I attend the hearing and state my case` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 119(2)(b), must the Commissioner decide my claim on equity, good conscience and the merits, without regard to technicalities` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 119(2)(b), must the Commissioner decide my claim on equity, good conscience and the merits, without regard to technicalities` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 121(2), s 122 (lines 4905-4915), s 124(1)(b) (lines 4941-4954), s 125(2) (lines 4976-4984), s 127A (lines 5246-5252)
#ASSERT `Under section 121(2), must I attend in person if the Commissioner thinks my employer would be prejudiced by my absence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Where the Commissioner is of the opinion that the interest of the employer or person liable is or is likely to be prejudiced" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `Under section 121(2), must I attend in person if the Commissioner thinks my employer would be prejudiced by my absence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Nothing in this Part limits or affects the jurisdiction of any court".
#ASSERT `Under section 122, does Part 15 limit the power of a court to hear a case about my employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 122, does Part 15 limit the power of a court to hear a case about my employment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A complaint to the Commissioner of a breach, and reason to believe the other person can give information.
#ASSERT `Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it` `s 124(1)(a) the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it` `s 124(1)(a) the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "whenever any person complains to a relevant authority of any breach" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): no complaint, and no other ground.
#ASSERT `Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it` `s 124(1)(a) the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone who is not one of the five named: the Act does not say that person may summon.
#ASSERT `Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it` `s 124(1)(a) some other person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 125(2), can the Commissioner join my complaint with other employees' similar complaints into one proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "In the event of there being more employees ... than one making a similar complaint, the Commissioner may, if the Commissioner institutes civil proceedings" (ruling (b); "in the event of" read as "where", assumed, fork F28): one complainant only.
#ASSERT `Under section 125(2), can the Commissioner join my complaint with other employees' similar complaints into one proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "No liability shall lie".
#ASSERT `Under section 127A, can I hold an officer of the Commissioner liable for something done with reasonable care and in good faith` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 127A, can I hold an officer of the Commissioner liable for something done with reasonable care and in good faith` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 133 (lines 5306-5314) and s 135 (lines 5327-5332)
#ASSERT `Under section 133, can the new Commissioner carry on my inquiry from where the earlier one left it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Where the Commissioner or any officer ... is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from concluding the inquiry" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): not prevented.
#ASSERT `Under section 133, can the new Commissioner carry on my inquiry from where the earlier one left it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No evidence taken down and no memorandum made (ruling (b), 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `Under section 133, can the new Commissioner carry on my inquiry from where the earlier one left it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Imprisonment served and ended, and no special provision to the contrary: the amount is deemed liquidated and discharged.
#ASSERT `Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it` TRUE `ea3 No` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A special provision to the contrary: the answer is that provision's.
#ASSERT `Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it` TRUE `ea3 Yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not sure whether a special provision applies: yes if none does, not given if one does.
#ASSERT `Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it` TRUE `ea3 I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it` FALSE `ea3 No` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 129(1) (lines 5263-5267) and s 137(1) (lines 5350-5372)
-- A person aggrieved may complain to a Magistrate's Court; no special provision to the contrary.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` `ea3 a Magistrate's Court` `ea3 No` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` `ea3 a District Court` `ea3 No` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to any special provision to the contrary": the answer is that provision's.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` `ea3 a District Court` `ea3 Yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not sure whether a special provision applies: yes if none does, not given if one does.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` `ea3 a District Court` `ea3 I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The section names the two courts and does not say that no other will do.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` `ea3 some other court` `ea3 No` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way` `s 137(1)(a) delivering it to the person or to some adult member of the person's family at the person's last known place of residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way` `s 137(1)(b) leaving it at, or sending it by registered post to, the person's usual or last known place of residence or business in an envelope addressed to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(c) where the person is a body of persons or a body corporate" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): the person asking is not one.
#ASSERT `Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way` `s 137(1)(c)(i) delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body at its registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The three ways are stated as how a summons "may be served" and the list is not closed with "only".
#ASSERT `Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way` `s 137(1) some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
